libraries to install:
        python3 -m pip install zmq
        python3 -m pip install pytz
Start message server first with (starts with ip 127.0.0.1 and port 5555)
    python3 message_server.py

assign the group servers by starting them (you can start multiple instances on different command line tabs)
    python3 group.py <ip> <port>

Eg.:python3 group.py 127.0.0.1 5556
    python3 group.py 127.0.0.1 5557
    (above example is for two group instances)

start the users as well by assigning uuid
    python3 user.py <uuid>
Eg.:python3 user.py 1
    python3 user.py 2

if two kernels start with the same uuid then the group will consider them as one entity/ treat them the same.

now you can use the user menu to perform actions

time is in HH::MM::SS format for input to get messages. (all messages after given time should be shown)

even if the user leaves the connection if he connects again assuming the group and message server did not shut down their information is retained

Since a user can join many groups he will have to enter the ip and port every time to specify which group he wants to mesage to. 
Similarly for leave and get message as well. ^ ^

